WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:07.349 align:start position:0%
 
[Applause]  we've been told to carry on planning for  christmas  and wear a mask while doing the shopping  the prime minister says we're going to  have a better festive period than last  year  but with the emergence of the omicron  variant how confident can we be  well we still don't have enough data  about the new variant and until we do  the health secretary says it makes sense  to have some measures in place there's  reason to to think that it may be and i  stress the word may that this variant  may turn out to make our vaccines less  effective it may not we just don't know  enough so i do think people will take  this more seriously and i think that  will apply to public transport it will  apply in shops it will be a regulation  as it has been before but it's important  i think to to act in a proportionate way  and also in a temporary way i hope this  is  something that we can remove within  within weeks  face masks and other interventions are  designed to buy the government time  time to understand more about this  variant  and time to slow its spread as news of  more omicron cases emerge in the uk  the health security agency has warned  numbers of this variant are expected to  rise we're showing that we're worried  about it by the actions that have been  rapidly taken by the uk government but  also by other governments around the  world it has more mutations than  anything we've seen before and some of  those mutations are in areas of the  virus that would particularly affect the  immune response  the government rejects any criticism  that it has not acted quickly enough in  imposing targeted border controls it  says all restrictions must be  proportional  but with another case linked to travel  discovered today from someone who  arrived in the uk and has now left again  do these restrictions really go far  enough there are still some outstanding  issues around travel the government is  saying everyone has to have a pcr test  on day two when they arrive back in the  uk but they're not suggesting  pre-departure tests for people before  they board flights there's no advice for  people about traveling back from the  airport on public transport  in addition to transport and shops masks  will have to be worn in english schools  all pupils in year 7 and above  and visitors to sites are required to  wear face coverings in communal areas  the national education union welcomed  the recommendation saying in a statement  we think the department for education  should go further and encourage mask  wearing in secondary classrooms and also  plan investment to improve ventilation  and air filtration these steps can all  help reduce the spread of covert and  thereby reduce disruption to education  the speed of the spread of the omicron  variant has to be matched by the speed  of action to try and slow it down  so far all three cases have been linked  to overseas travel  there is no proof of community  transmission yet  if and when that happens  then a rethink on interventions  will be needed  joshi sky news

